{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794603389,"nonce":"3OwFx7nT3g+FRUDrtbR/nQNGtBQ=","message":"Measured, step 1 of the list above (72b3f779): crates/blinc_recorder/tests/animation_paths.rs now has a scene each for the cn collapsible section, accordion, tree, sidebar and tabs, driven by their own state (a signal, or a click on the tree row), 30 frames of 16 ms. `the_cn_disclosure_scenes_animate` checks that each moves (the picture changes in 14 to 16 frames and by more than 200 px end to end), so a scene cannot go vacuous. `how_the_cn_disclosures_are_painted` (ignored, `--run-ignored all --no-capture`, BLINC_ANIM_PATHS_SCALE=2 for retina) reports how each frame was painted.\n\nResult, all five, at 1x and 2x, and on all three paths (full paint, promoted and patched, rows on the CPU): every moving frame is a full paint, 15 of 15 each. The frames after the animation ends are cached. So the claim above holds for the compositor's gate in the harness, and nothing in them is on rows or on the fast path.\n\nWhat a moving frame costs in these scenes (320 x 240, a handful of rows, median of the moving frames): collapsible 3.7 ms, accordion 3.3 to 4.7, tree 3.4 to 4.2, tabs 4.4 to 4.7, sidebar 7.5 to 9.3 at 1x and 6.6 at 2x. These are tiny trees. The cost that matters is a full paint of the screen the animation is in: cn_profile measures a full paint of cn_demo at 28 to 43 ms and a layout pass of 1 to 5 ms in the same harness (the first full paint 1.2 s). Every frame of an accordion or tree opening in cn_demo is therefore about that, not 3 ms; I did not run the animation inside cn_demo itself, so that is an estimate from the two figures.\n\nWhere cn_demo hits them (call sites in cn_demo.rs): tabs 3, accordion 2, tree_view 2, sidebar 1, toasts 8, drawers 3, dialogs 2 (the toast tray and overlay stack animate through their own animate_bounds). collapsible is used by accordion and the tree rather than directly. Not measured: the overlay stack and toast tray (dialog, drawer, toast open and close), which are the most used.\n\nWhat each animation is, from the cn source, which decides what a row can carry:\n- collapsible, accordion body and tree group: `VisualAnimationConfig::height().clip_to_animated()` on a clipped body, content built at its final size. The visible change is a clip that grows plus a translate of everything below, in the tree also the `position()` animation of each row shell. That is a clip row and translate rows: no reflow of the content.\n- tabs indicator: `VisualAnimationConfig::all().shared()` on a pill that slides and resizes between triggers: a translate and a size change of one node with a background. A scale of a rounded pill distorts its corners, so this one needs the size or a repaint of the one node.\n- sidebar: collapsing changes the width and the labels hide, so content reflows; it is the layout animation case, not a row.\n\nNext: do the accordion, collapsible and tree as rows (clip row plus translate rows), since they are the common ones and need no size delta; leave tabs and sidebar for after, and measure the overlay stack and toasts first.","files":null}]}